file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h1_dataset.dta saved

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         * only keep participants from private households
.         keep if inlist(pop,1,2)
(89,279 observations deleted)

. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * generate dummy variable for whether participant has at least one da
> ughter (1) or not (0)
.         gen d_daughter = (kidsex01==2|kidsex02==2|kidsex03==2|kidsex04==2|kid
> sex05==2|kidsex06==2|kidsex07==2|kidsex08==2|kidsex09==2|kidsex10==2|kidsex11
> ==2|kidsex12==2|kidsex13==2|kidsex14==2|kidsex15==2|kidsex16==2|kidsex17==2|k
> idsex18==2|kidsex19==2)

. 
.         *Proxy for support for gender equality: agreement with: Schools and p
> reschools should promote non-gender-typical activities that are not typical f
> or children’s gender
.         gen gender_att = plh0395i05
(67,373 missing values generated)

. 
.         *generate control variables
.         *male DV
.         gen male=sex==1

.         *age=survey year-birth year
.         gen age=syear-gebjahr

.         *immigrant status DV =1 if born overseas, 0 if born in germany or imm
> ig <1950
.         gen immig_status=germborn==2

.         *log net household income
.         gen log_income=log(hghinc)
(30,708 missing values generated)

.         *total number of years of education
.         gen edu=pgbilzeit
(62,122 missing values generated)

. 
.         global controls "age male immig_status log_income edu"

. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here: linear OLS regr
> ession
.         * Using plh0395i05 as measure of support for gender equality (agreeme
> nt with: Schools and preschools should promote non-gender-typical activities 
> that are not typical for children’s gender).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with plh0395i0
> 5 as dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter as independent vari
> able
. 
.         reg gender_att d_daughter $controls if edu>=0 & gender_att>0 & gender
> _att!=., r

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =     21,357
                                                F(6, 21350)       =     180.43
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0000
                                                R-squared         =     0.0473
                                                Root MSE          =     1.8969

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
  gender_att | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |   .0494988    .027471     1.80   0.072    -.0043464     .103344
         age |   .0025899   .0008182     3.17   0.002     .0009861    .0041938
        male |    -.65422   .0262737   -24.90   0.000    -.7057183   -.6027216
immig_status |  -.4164735   .0418433    -9.95   0.000    -.4984895   -.3344575
  log_income |   .0294685   .0229901     1.28   0.200    -.0155939    .0745309
         edu |   .0701879   .0049137    14.28   0.000     .0605567     .079819
       _cons |   4.194823   .1807314    23.21   0.000     3.840576     4.54907
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_d_daughter = _b[d_daughter]

.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
.         // Display the saved statistics
.         di "Coefficient: `coefficient'"
Coefficient: .0494987849479333

.         di "Standard Error: `se'"
Standard Error: .0274709836429709

.         di "Test Statistic Family: `test_stat_family'"
Test Statistic Family: t

.         di "Residual Degrees of Freedom: `df_residual'"
Residual Degrees of Freedom: 21350

.         di "Model Degrees of Freedom: `df_model'"
Model Degrees of Freedom: 6

.         di "p-value: " `p_value'
p-value: .071582

.         di "Number of observations: " `num_obs'
Number of observations: 21357

.         di      "Number of participants: " `num_participants'
Number of participants: 21357

.         di "Interpretation of directionality: " "`interpretation'"
Interpretation of directionality: positive coefficient is in line with hypothes
> is

